WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.800
AI is smart.

00:00:01.955 --> 00:00:03.625
But the way we use it?

00:00:03.706 --> 00:00:05.422
It's frustratingly dumb.

00:00:05.785 --> 00:00:07.608
It doesn't know what's new.

00:00:07.794 --> 00:00:10.642
It rewrites code that already exists.

00:00:10.731 --> 00:00:13.870
And it has trouble with long-horizon tasks.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.011
Bigger models alone won't fix this.

00:00:17.856 --> 00:00:22.339
Teleion Fabric is a fabric of OmniNodes that keeps evolving.

00:00:22.442 --> 00:00:26.008
It takes a different shape for each request.

00:00:26.979 --> 00:00:30.798
Meta's Muse models help power the fabric.

00:00:31.752 --> 00:00:36.901
A small Meta-based decider picks the model for real Tasks.

00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:43.172
A fine-tuned Meta model helps power it too, served through several routes.

00:00:45.156 --> 00:00:49.545
It runs on any model, including Meta models.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:55.032
It keeps getting better at new events, code reuse and long tasks.

00:00:56.675 --> 00:00:59.542
Long work becomes small Tasks in a queue.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:04.325
Finished work stays as Task Objects the next agent reuses.

00:01:06.368 --> 00:01:08.278
Every run is recorded.

00:01:08.528 --> 00:01:12.619
Over time, it works out the right harness, model, skills, tools

00:01:12.649 --> 00:01:17.836
and hooks for each Task, and when plain code is enough.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:24.276
In our testing, a repeated job used far fewer tokens.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.214
One run needed no model at all.

00:01:28.937 --> 00:01:30.411
And we measure it.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:36.124
Correct answers about new GitHub projects went from 0 to 26 of 30.

00:01:36.854 --> 00:01:40.232
It wrote about 16 percent less code.

00:01:40.562 --> 00:01:45.895
After a crash, work restarted with 7 model calls, not 10.

00:01:47.025 --> 00:01:49.484
And this is running right now.

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:58.554
Teleion Fabric can run almost anything, and we decided to put it to work, with Eranos.

00:01:58.938 --> 00:02:06.791
A nonprofit presses My NGO needs help, and says what it needs.

00:02:07.558 --> 00:02:12.645
It can be a cited report, or a reusable process.

00:02:13.223 --> 00:02:18.085
Agents pick up the work, one small Task at a time.

00:02:18.935 --> 00:02:25.301
Anyone with spare AI can press I want to help, and connect their agent.

00:02:26.027 --> 00:02:31.897
Then a separate worker audits and approves the result, and every point links to its source.

00:02:32.623 --> 00:02:39.166
The team decides what to use, and every solution joins a free library.

00:02:39.481 --> 00:02:42.080
See it at eranosforgood.org.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:51.074
Open one, and press Adapt it for my group.

00:02:52.874 --> 00:02:54.531
AI is smart.

00:02:54.803 --> 00:02:57.391
Now the way we use it can be smart too.

00:02:57.764 --> 00:02:59.500
Connect your agents today.

